d_at":"2026-10-13T08:04:53Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/parisxmas/fastroute/releases/download/v0.1.14/fastroute-kicad-0.1.14.zip"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/parisxmas/fastroute/releases/assets/705720124","id":705720124,"node_id":"RA_kwDOUzXdlM4qEG88","name":"SHA256SUMS.txt","label":"","uploader":{"login":"parisxmas","id":7112725,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTI3MjU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7112725?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/parisxmas","html_url":"https://github.com/parisxmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/parisxmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/parisxmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/parisxmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/parisxmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/parisxmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/parisxmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/parisxmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/parisxmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/parisxmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"text/plain; charset=utf-8","state":"uploaded","size":697,"digest":"sha256:629cdd213b32ab9990418af744f226421506a80788152231f70b29d60e1e750a","download_count":2,"created_at":"2026-11-03T13:31:59Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T13:31:59Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/parisxmas/fastroute/releases/download/v0.1.14/SHA256SUMS.txt"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/parisxmas/fastroute/tarball/v0.1.14","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/parisxmas/fastroute/zipball/v0.1.14","body":"Two bug fixes contributed by @sulkaharo: a panic in differential pair length matching and a clearance violation created by trace-end bridges. `--parity` still reproduces Freerouting bit for bit.\n\n## Downloads\n\n| File | For |\n|---|---|\n| `fastroute-kicad-0.1.14.zip` | **KiCad plugin** (KiCad 7 or newer). Bundles fastroute for Windows x64, macOS (Apple Silicon and Intel) and Linux (x64, arm64). Install with *Plugin and Content Manager → Install from File…* — do not unzip. |\n| `fastroute-0.1.14-<platform>.tar.gz` / `.zip` | Command line binary only: `fastroute -de board.dsn -do board.ses` |\n| `SHA256SUMS.txt` | Checksums |\n\n## Pair length matching: panic fixed (#4)\n\nWith `--pairs`, the length-matching stage after routing could panic with `RationalPoint is not an IntPoint`. It happened in 3 of 5 runs on a 6-layer board with two pairs. A meander rebuilt the whole trace from its corners, and any corner where two any-angle lines meet is not an integer point. A line drawn through such a corner panicked. The meander now keeps the trace's own lines and replaces only the line of the segment it bends, so no line is ever drawn through an existing corner.\n\n## Trace-end bridges stay inside the pad (#5, fixes #3)\n\nA trace end that lies inside a same-net pad or via but off its centre is joined to the centre by a short bridge. The bridge was inserted at the trace's full width, so a trace wider than the pad put new copper outside the pad, within clearance of other nets. That copper was then reported as a *pre-existing, unfixable* violation (measured on a real board: a 0.6 mm trunk bridged into a small resistor pad, 0.100 mm from another net at clearance 0.15 mm). The bridge's width is now capped so it stays inside the pad's copper. A bridge with no room is skipped.\n","mentions_count":1}